1
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:12,000
Some sagas just won't die.

2
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:18,000
Vampires Suck is a comedy, fantasy film directed by Aaron Seltzer.

3
00:12:18,000 --> 00:12:24,000
Becca, an anxious, non-vampire teen is torn between two boys.

4
00:16:24,000 --> 00:16:30,000
Before she can choose, Becca must get around her
controlling father, who treats her like a child.

5
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:36,000
Meanwhile, Becca's friends contend with their own romantic
issues – all of which collide at the prom.

6
00:24:36,000 --> 00:24:42,000
Becca Crane, played by Jenn Proske.

7
00:28:42,000 --> 00:28:48,000
Edward, played by Matt Lanter.

8
00:32:48,000 --> 00:32:54,000
Jacob White, played by Chris Riggi.

9
00:36:54,000 --> 00:37:00,000
Frank Crane, played by Diedrich Bader.

10
00:41:00,000 --> 00:41:06,000
Jennifer, played by Anneliese Van Der Pol.

11
00:45:06,000 --> 00:45:12,000
Daro, played by Ken Jeong.

12
00:49:12,000 --> 00:49:18,000
Vampires Suck is a 2010 American parody film written and
directed by Jason Friedberg and Aaron Seltzer.

13
00:53:18,000 --> 00:53:24,000
It stars Jenn Proske, Matt Lanter, Christopher N.

14
00:57:24,000 --> 00:57:30,000
Riggi, Ken Jeong, Anneliese van der Pol, and Arielle Kebbel.

15
01:01:30,000 --> 01:01:36,000
The film is a parody of The Twilight Saga franchise (mainly
the original film and its sequel, New Moon).

16
01:05:36,000 --> 01:05:42,000
Like the previous Friedberg and Seltzer movies, the film was
panned by critics for its humor and plot.

17
01:09:42,000 --> 01:09:48,000
20th Century Fox theatrically released the film on August 18, 2010.

18
01:13:48,000 --> 01:13:54,000
The film explores themes of high school, vampire, parody, spoof, prom.

19
01:17:54,000 --> 01:18:00,000
The tone is lighthearted.
